      "title": "House of Abhinandan Lodha prepays ₹1,100 crore loan to HDFC Capital",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/house-of-abhinandan-lodha-prepays-1-100-crore-loan-to-hdfc-capital-126111500404_1.html",
      "description": "Real estate firm The House of Abhinandan Lodha (HoABL) has prepaid a Rs 1,100 crore loan to private equity firm HDFC Capital, which it had raised to develop housing projects, comprising mainly plots.\nIn a statement on Sunday, HoABL said it has given an exit to HDFC Capital Advisors Ltd across many projects by making a payment of Rs 1,100 crore as the principal amount before the due date.\nIn 2023, HoABL partnered with HDFC Capital to set up a joint platform to invest in plotted developments and low-rise projects located in metros, Tier II cities and emerging markets in India.\nHDFC Capital had committed around Rs 1,500 crore to the platform across 11 projects.\nTo date, HoABL has returned around Rs 1,100 crore to HDFC Capital under the platform.\nVipul Roongta, CEO of HDFC Capital, said, \"HoABL is a new-age real estate company, which has successfully created a differentiated real estate niche, particularly through plotted developments, low-rise projects and focus on affordable and ...",
